{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"King Nimi’s Conduct","html":"<article id='cp6'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Cariyāpiṭaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Conduct Leading to Buddhahood </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Akittivagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Chapter With Akitti </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Dānapāramī 6 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Perfection of Giving (6th) </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Nimirājacariya </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>King Nimi’s Conduct </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Punāparaṁ yadā homi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“Then again when I was </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>mithilāyaṁ puruttame; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>in the capital city of Mithilā </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Nimi nāma mahārājā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I was the great king named Nimi, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>paṇḍito kusalatthiko. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>astute and seeking the good. </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tadāhaṁ māpayitvāna, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Then having had constructed </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>catussālaṁ catummukhaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>four halls with four openings, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tattha dānaṁ pavattesiṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I provided gifts there </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>migapakkhinarādinaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>for beasts, birds, men, and so forth. </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Acchādanañca sayanaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Clothing and beds, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>annaṁ pānañca bhojanaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>food and drink to enjoy: </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Abbocchinnaṁ karitvāna, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I provided them without let, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>mahādānaṁ pavattayiṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>performing a great offering. </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yathāpi sevako sāmiṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Suppose a servant is looking </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>dhanahetumupāgato; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>to get a raise from their boss, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kāyena vācā manasā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>they’d seek to fulfill their needs </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>ārādhanīyamesati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>by body, speech, and mind. </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tathevāhaṁ sabbabhave, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>In that way in every life </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>pariyesissāmi bodhijaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I shall seek the wisdom born of awakening. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Dānena satte tappetvā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Having pleased beings with gifts, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>icchāmi bodhimuttaman”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I wish for the supreme awakening.” </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Nimirājacariyaṁ chaṭṭhaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
